                <pb facs="0501" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4310: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-19T14:00:00-05:00">February 19, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. For the Minister and the Consul General. Reference Minister’s February 18, 11
                    p.m., in regard to Japanese ultimatum, and Minister’s telegram of February 18, 8
                    p.m., sent from U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Houston</hi>, last sentence.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department approves the Consul General warning Americans residing in
                        Hongkew to avoid places where danger of shelling exists.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Although it has not been and is not Department’s policy to evacuate
                        American nationals from Shanghai or to discuss possibility of evacuation
                        short of a state of extreme emergency, Department assumes that all
                        practicable measures are being taken (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) for
                        removal of Americans from endangered regions and (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >b</hi>) for possible ultimate evacuation, in case it should become
                        necessary, from Shanghai. Please telegraph what arrangements have been made
                        or are under discussion and what steps the authorities of other countries
                        have taken or are discussing.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
